design/coupling-signal  warn (heuristic)  internal/jit/compile.go:350:1
  owner:       jit::compile#function
  message:     function coordinates 14 collaborators in its package
  requirement: Coupling SHOULD be judged from direct intra-package fan-in and fan-out, that is the functions and methods of the same package that call a symbol or are called by it, against deliberately high thresholds. Calls from other packages and from tests do not count: a widely used public function is a service, not a hub.
  intent:      A dependency hub changes for many reasons.
  evidence:    callees=["a","b c"] fan_in=2 fan_out=14
  expected:    valid go example `ordinary-fan` (sample.go)
                 package sample

                 func hub() {
                 	left()
                 	right()
                 }

                 func left()  {}
                 func right() {}

                 func a() { hub() }
                 func b() { hub() }
  fingerprint: f5ed6fd96750ace1775528b31f2cdc85a58b8b9bb1222cd4e3d4bd9d6d9f8bfd

design/private-helper-callers  review (heuristic)  src/lib.rs:7:1
  owner:       m::helper#function
  message:     private helper has one caller
  requirement: A private helper SHOULD have at least two callers.
  intent:      A private helper with one caller is usually part of that caller.
  expected:    valid rust example `rust-valid` (src/lib.rs)
                 pub fn run(x: u8) -> u8 {
                     clamp(x) + 1
                 }

                 pub fn other(x: u8) -> u8 {
                     clamp(x) + 2
                 }

                 fn clamp(x: u8) -> u8 {
                     if x > 10 { 10 } else { x }
                 }
